VeridianOS: port the agent's async result from GSimpleAsyncResult to GTask

GCC reported -Wdeprecated-declarations for g_simple_async_result_new()
(agent/polkitqtlistener.cpp), g_simple_async_result_complete() and
g_simple_async_result_set_error() (agent/polkitqt1-agent-session.cpp) and
g_simple_async_result_propagate_error() (agent/listeneradapter.cpp).
GSimpleAsyncResult is deprecated since GLib 2.46 in favour of GTask, which
the project's minimum GLib (2.36) already has.

The change:
- polkit_qt_listener_initiate_authentication() creates the result with
  g_task_new() on the same source object, callback and user data. No
  cancellable is attached, as before: a GTask with one would turn a
  cancelled request into G_IO_ERROR_CANCELLED on its own, whereas
  cancellation is handled through cancelled_cb and the agent still
  completes the request. The source tag stays agent_listener, as before.
- AsyncResult holds a GTask. GTask returns an error together with the
  completion, so setError() keeps the GError and setCompleted() returns it
  with g_task_return_error(), or g_task_return_boolean(TRUE) when there was
  none. The usage contract (setError() then setCompleted()) is unchanged.
- initiate_authentication_finish() returns g_task_propagate_boolean():
  FALSE with the error set if the agent reported one, TRUE otherwise, as
  before.

Interface change: AsyncResult's constructor (public header
agent/polkitqt1-agent-session.h, documented \internal) and the private
ListenerAdapter method now take a GTask * instead of a GSimpleAsyncResult *.
Only polkit-qt-1 itself constructs AsyncResult; agents such as
polkit-kde-agent-1 only receive one and call setError()/setCompleted(),
which are unchanged.

Behaviour differences: when an agent completes the request from inside
initiateAuthentication() itself (e.g. polkit-kde-agent's "another client is
already authenticating" path), GTask delivers the callback from an idle on
the next main-context iteration instead of re-entrantly, as GIO requires of
async results; and an AsyncResult destroyed without ever being completed
now makes GLib report it as a critical warning (g_critical: the GTask was
finalized without returning; the request was left unanswered before as
well).

